# Cross-OS line-ending contract.
#
# This repo is edited on Windows and executed on Linux (DCCN cluster) with the
# working tree mirrored by Mutagen, which syncs bytes verbatim. A CRLF working
# tree therefore reaches the cluster as CRLF and breaks shebangs ("bash\r:
# No such file or directory") and Slurm #SBATCH parsing. Forcing LF in both the
# index AND the working tree is what keeps the two sides byte-identical.
#
# Pair this with `git config core.autocrlf input` locally (already set).

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary artefacts -- never touch these. The .mat files are byte-frozen SPM12
# parity fixtures; any normalisation would silently corrupt the v0.8.0 gates.
*.mat  binary
*.pt   binary
*.pth  binary
*.npz  binary
*.npy  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.db    binary
*.sqlite binary
